=== SURVEY ===
Web source FullscreenButton.tsx is a single ghost icon-`Button` that wraps the browser Fullscreen
API (`requestFullscreen` / `exitFullscreen` / `fullscreenchange` / `document.fullscreenEnabled`).
Contract (from the module doc + test file):
  • Support gate — hides itself entirely when `document.fullscreenEnabled === false` (iOS Safari /
    sandboxed iframe), with a `testHookSupported` override seam. No pseudo-fullscreen fallback.
  • State source — `isFs` is sourced from the `fullscreenchange` event, NOT the click handler, so it
    stays honest on Esc-out / system revoke / a sibling toggling the same target.
  • Active detection — `el === target || target.contains(el)` (a descendant counts).
  • toggle() — no target → no-op; ours/descendant active → exit; a foreign lock → exit-then-request;
    nothing active → request. A rejected `requestFullscreen()` is caught → `console.warn`, UI un-flipped.
  • Label / icon / aria flip together — `isFs ? <Minimize/> : <Maximize/>`,
    `isFs ? exitLabel : enterLabel`, `aria-pressed = isFs`, `title = aria-label`. Enter/exit labels are
    overridable (`ariaLabelEnter` / `ariaLabelExit`).
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation only (no network, no data-fetch hook). Shared components: none
(it composes the web `Button`). Charts/maps: none.
i18n keys extracted from source: common.fullscreen.enter ("Enter fullscreen"),
common.fullscreen.exit ("Exit fullscreen").
Existing native: no FullscreenButton / FullscreenPresenting / FullscreenButtonModel symbols
(grep = 0 collisions). The sibling ChartContainer surface draws its OWN inline fullscreen toggle
(ChartContainerFullscreenButton) against an `expanded` binding — distinct type, no clash; this prompt
ships the standalone reusable primitive the web `FullscreenButton` is.
Canonical surface pattern studied: shared-surfaces/CopyButton (0207) — the closest analog: a button
primitive wrapping a platform API behind a Seams layer, with Model/Seams/Views/Previews/strings/
Tests/ModelTests + an @Observable state-holder + an os.Logger view.opened seam.

=== REASONING ===
- The web component delegates the actual fullscreen rendering to the browser and only (a) probes
  support, (b) reads the live fullscreen element, (c) requests/exits, and (d) flips its icon+label.
  The native parity keeps that exact separation: a `FullscreenPresenting` seam is the native shape of
  the Fullscreen API (the single, observable source of truth for "which element is fullscreen" — the
  parity of `document.fullscreenElement` + `fullscreenchange`); the host surface (the native parity of
  the web `targetRef` element — a chart card / map container) presents the enlarged content
  (fullScreenCover on iOS, full-screen window on macOS) by observing the published `activeTargetID`.
- Every web branch is reproduced as pure, unit-tested logic (icon switch, label resolution, active
  detection incl. descendant, the 4-way toggle decision) + the @MainActor model that drives the
  presenter and logs a rejected request (web `catch`). The view is a pure function of `isSupported` +
  `isFullscreen` + `resolvedLabel`.
- The generic data-feed leaf states (loading / empty / stale / offline / error-retry) named in the
  prompt template DO NOT apply to a stateless, networkless presentation-toggle primitive whose only
  hook is useTranslation — they are intentionally absent rather than faked, the documented precedent
  of the sibling action surfaces ChartExportMenu 0066 / CopyLinkButton 0168 / CopyButton 0207. The
  states reproduced are the ACTUAL ones the web source renders (see PARITY below).

=== PARITY (web branch -> native) ===
  unsupported  -> model.isSupported == false -> view renders nothing      (web `if (!supported) return null`)
  resting      -> isFullscreen == false -> "arrow.up.left.and.arrow.down.right" + "Enter fullscreen", pressed=false
  active       -> isFullscreen == true  -> "arrow.down.right.and.arrow.up.left" + "Exit fullscreen",  pressed=true (.isSelected)
  detached     -> targetID == nil -> button renders, toggle no-ops        (web `if (!target) return`)
  external/Esc -> presenter.activeTargetID changes -> view re-renders      (web `fullscreenchange` listener)
  descendant   -> descendantIDs.contains(active) -> reported active        (web `target.contains(el)`)
  arbitration  -> foreign lock -> presenter.exit() then request()          (web exit-then-request)
  rejected     -> presenter.request()==false -> os.Logger.warning, no flip (web `catch` -> console.warn)
  labels       -> enter/exit overridable                                   (web `ariaLabelEnter`/`ariaLabelExit`)
  i18n         -> common.fullscreen.enter / .exit via NSLocalizedString     (web `t(key, default)`)
  className     : Tailwind seam, no native analogue — styling via P1/S9 tokens through TSButton (absent by design)
PARITY_COVERED == PARITY_REQUIRED (data + behaviour + every state + native-chrome i18n reproduced).

